      "stop_reason": "agent_finished",
      "final_text": "All 4 tests now pass. I fixed four defects:\n\n- **`Reservation.active` in `models.py`:** the comparison was inverted (`now >= expires_at`). It is now `now < expires_at`, so a reservation holds stock only before it expires.\n- **`reserve` in `store.py`:** it compared the requested quantity against total stock. It now compares against `available(sku)`, so units held by active reservations count.\n- **`release` in `store.py`:** it raised `KeyError` for an unknown id. It now does `pop(rid, None)`, so releasing twice is harmless.\n- **`commit` in `store.py`:** it didn't check expiry, which the docstring requires. It now raises `KeyError` for an expired reservation and leaves stock unchanged. No test covers this, so it's the one change the test run doesn't confirm.",
